    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Implement Hybrid Logic\r\n\r\n\r\n**Task 3 Goal:** Protect the user from errors by trying to fetch live data first, then falling back to your safety net if it fails.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. **Clean Up:**\r\n\t* **Delete** the line `renderBackup();` from the bottom of your code.\r\n\t* **Keep** the line `renderAppShell();`. We still want the header to load instantly!\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Create an `async` arrow function named `fetchCountries`. Inside, add a `try { } catch (error) { }` block.\r\n\r\n3. Inside `try`:\r\n    * Update the `statusElement` text to read \"Online. Showing Live Data.\"\r\n    * Use `fetch` to get data from the `apiEndpoint` and display the `name.common` and `population` of each country in the `outputElement`. \r\n\r\n4. Inside `catch`:\r\n    * Update the `statusElement` text to read \"Offline Mode. Showing Local Data\".\r\n    * Call your `renderBackup()` function.\r\n\r\n5. Add an event listener so that clicking the \"Get Live Census\" button runs your `fetchCountries` function.\r\n",
